WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.635
-My first guest tonight
is one of the

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.636
biggest stars in the world.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.970
She's a talented
actor and producer,

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.807
who's just released her memoir,
called "Unfinished."

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:11.978
It is available now.
Here is Priyanka Chopra Jonas!

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.848
Priyanka,
it is so good to see you.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.783
Look at this.
-It's so good to be back.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.184
Real book, man. Look at that.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.588
-Hey, by the way, not
double-spaced, not a crazy font.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.890
-Not pictorial, not a comic.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.726
You know, like,
real words, sentences. Damn!

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.828
-Great stories. Amazing.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.429
I got to hop in.
I got to get into this.

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:31.831
I have so many questions.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.000
You've had a
very productive quarantine.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.302
You've had two movies.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.338
Well, I mean, because,
you know, I'm a fan.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:42.675
You've had two movies come out
on Netflix, giant hits.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:46.312
You filmed two movies
and an Amazon series.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:50.483
And you finished a memoir about
your life up to this point.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:54.554
I'm sorry.
Some people made bread, okay?

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.690
-I was home for six months,
and that's when

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.525
the book happened,
is when I wrote --

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:01.428
I wrote the book
during quarantine.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.262
But, you know,
there's so many people

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:06.165
watching movies and content
that, you know,

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.200
our industry is back at work.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.771
I went back to work in October
and finished two movies.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.873
I'm starting my new TV show.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.476
But, you know, I'm just grateful
to be back at work, honestly.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:20.646
It's been such a dreary time for
everyone, being stuck at home,

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:24.050
and I feel grateful
to be able to, you know,

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.318
keep creating content at a time
when people really need it.

00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:27.553
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.288
By the way, I was going to
thank you for that,

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:31.124
because, seriously,
we do need content,

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:34.260
and anyone who is
giving it to us, thank you.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.995
We love it.
-Including you.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.297
Thank you for
going back to the studio.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:40.466
-I'm happy to talk to you.
I'm happy to talk to people.

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:42.235
It's just great.
And to see other people.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.369
-People are great.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.738
-I know.
It's like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.941
You and your husband,
Nick Jonas, who we love --

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:51.343
you usually travel
a lot for work.

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:54.480
But it must have been really
nice to have more time together.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.182
It's, like,
really kind of interesting.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.283
-It's amazing.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.451
I mean,
it would have never happened.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.820
We both have such
crazy individual careers.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.089
I don't think
I have ever been home

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.591
for six months
in almost 25 years.

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:06.759
-Last time he was on,

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:12.131
he was showing me his
Baby Shark workout.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:15.534
Dude, it's tough.
Dude, he's in great shape, man.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.803
Do you guys work out together?

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.372
-Initially, you know,
I'm not someone

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.375
who's a fan of working out,
like most people,

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:26.111
but when you're married
to him, you know,

00:02:26.111 --> 00:02:28.281
he wakes up in the morning
bright-eyed, bushy-tailed,

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:32.284
and he'll wear his
workout gear and go to do it.

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:35.121
So, you know, someone like me,
who's laying in bed

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.989
and been watching TikToks
for an hour,

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:39.192
is like,
"Alright, I'm just gonna --

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.794
I'm gonna get up
and try this thing."

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.797
But then he goes and makes you
do the Baby Shark workout,

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:48.234
and I'm thinking, like, pop
songs and we're going to dance.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.869
And it's not easy.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.572
I stopped -- I gave up competing
with him a long time ago.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:56.709
-Yeah. I want to talk about this
book, "Unfinished."

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.545
Congratulations.
It is out today.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:00.914
It became a best seller within

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.882
a day of being available
for pre-orders,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.917
so congratulations.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.618
It's already a best seller.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.787
How does it feel
to finally have this out?

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.690
I mean, this is amazing stories.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.392
How did you
remember these stories?

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:15.494
-I had to remind myself to
remember it, honestly.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.630
I didn't remember a lot of it.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.399
But having that pause during
quarantine really helped.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.368
But, also,
it's a little strange.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:25.371
You know, I've been --
I mean, I've just gotten to know

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.873
a lot of people here
in America recently.

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:32.078
But I've had a career in the
public eye for almost 20 years,

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:34.246
and I've taught myself to,
you know,

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:37.383
be very private and be
ferociously protective of it.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.852
And then I do this crazy thing
and write a book.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.821
I mean, what was I thinking?
I don't know.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:44.824
-No, but they're great stories.
-I know.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.959
-The one is, you know,
20 years ago.

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:49.028
You won Ms. World.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.563
And we have
a photo of you winning.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:51.831
-Yep.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:54.400
-You must have a thousand things
going in your brain.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.037
But in the book, there's a great
story about your hair.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.404
Can we show the photo
one more time?

00:03:59.404 --> 00:04:01.641
Why it's styled this way.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:04.410
You go, "Oh, just 'cause she's
gorgeous and it beautiful."

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.312
But that's not the case.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.882
-No, I have this
crazy tendril down my face,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.485
and at that time,
I tried to play it cool

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.954
as if it was like a choice,
but it really wasn't.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.222
I was trying to curl my hair,

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:18.223
and there was like
90 girls backstage.

00:04:18.223 --> 00:04:19.659
Everyone is moving around

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.693
and getting their
hair and makeup done.

00:04:21.693 --> 00:04:23.862
And I was trying to curl
my hair, and -- I don't know --

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:28.534
somebody jostled me, and I burnt
myself and the skin scabbed.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.670
So I had, like, this big mark,

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:35.675
which I had to conceal with
concealer and that big tendril.

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:39.211
-And you're in the Ms. World
competition. Hello!

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:41.447
-Every time I look back at that
picture, I'm like,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:44.550
"The choice of
the tendril -- really?"

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.420
-I think -- Well, it worked.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:52.358
There's so many great stories,
and emotional stories, too,

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.026
that I love knowing about you.

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:57.697
But one thing that --
Just the cover.

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:59.965
Can you tell everyone
the story about the tattoo

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:02.334
right there on your wrist
or is it too --

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:07.739
I mean, I get emotional
thinking about it myself.

00:05:07.739 --> 00:05:09.374
-I was very close to my father.

00:05:09.374 --> 00:05:12.745
He was my greatest champion,
my biggest cheerleader,

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.346
like, the loudest guy
in the room.

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:16.515
You know, if I'd win an award,
he'd be like, "Ahh!"

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:17.784
And I had to tell him,
"Dad, you know,

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:19.285
you've got to play it cool now."

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.686
But dad didn't know how to.

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:23.922
He was just, like, so excited
about everything I did.

00:05:23.922 --> 00:05:29.962
And when he died, it was just
quiet in that corner, you know?

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:32.999
In that corner of cheer.
-Yeah.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:35.901
-Even though I have
a very supportive family,

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:38.738
but they weren't all as
rambunctious as him, you know?

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:44.877
And this tattoo was -- I got it
about a year or two before

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:48.381
my dad passed, and I lied
to him and I told him

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:49.549
I needed to write this down

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:52.318
because I wanted it
for artwork for my album.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:54.553
But he wrote it
in his handwriting,

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:56.689
and it's my first tattoo.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:06:00.258
And, you know,
now I have it here with me.

00:06:00.258 --> 00:06:01.627
-"Daddy's lil girl..."

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:04.230
I just thought it's so cool

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:07.733
and it's a great way
to remember him.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:09.635
And you know
he's rooting for you right now.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.736
He's going crazy.

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:13.339
He's going like,
"Two movies and a memoir?!

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:17.242
You go, go, go!"

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:21.147
I know you're very close
with your family.

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:24.884
In one of the stories, to show
how supportive they were --

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.885
By the way, you look
just like your mother.

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:28.654
Oh, my gosh.
-I do?

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:30.923
-Oh, yes. Absolutely.
-Oh, that's great.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.792
-Yeah.
-I really want to tell her that.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:35.327
-Yeah.
-I really wanted to. Thank you.

00:06:35.327 --> 00:06:39.665
-But one of the stories --
it's towards the end --

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:43.236
talking about how they
let you be an individual,

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:45.270
even when you
were just a young kid.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:46.405
There were these placards

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:49.541
outside of your home
where you grew up?

00:06:49.541 --> 00:06:53.312
-You know, we lived in
a military home,

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:54.747
so all the houses
looked the same

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:56.448
and they always had,
like, nameplates,

00:06:56.448 --> 00:06:58.617
we used to call them,
where the officers

00:06:58.617 --> 00:07:00.852
and their names
and their designations

00:07:00.852 --> 00:07:02.854
would be written
outside the house.

00:07:02.854 --> 00:07:05.424
Because both my parents
were in the military,

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:08.360
it was, you know,
"Major Chopra,"

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:11.197
his designation --
MD, MBBS, whatever --

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:15.868
my mom's, "Captain Chopra."

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:18.771
And I remember when that
nameplate was being put up,

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:21.874
I was 5 years old, in
kindergarten at that point.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:25.144
And I asked my dad,
very innocently --

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:27.580
I was like, "Don't I live
in this house, too?

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.715
Why isn't my name up there?"

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:33.218
And at 5 --
-How cute is that?

00:07:33.218 --> 00:07:36.689
5-year-old little Priyanka
going, "Wait.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:38.157
Where's my nameplate?
Do I not live here?"

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:39.625
-"I live here, too."

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:42.962
-"Do I not matter to you guys?
Hello?"

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:47.633
-And instead of laughing at me,
my dad said, "You are right.

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.602
We are going to
amend this nameplate."

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:54.540
And he wrote
"Ms. Priyanka Chopra, Upper KG"

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.708
for "kindergarten."

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:58.243
-Kindergarten.
I thought that was the best.

00:07:58.243 --> 00:08:02.548
You -- Go, great, mom and dad.
I love that you did that.

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:04.049
It's just you.

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:05.651
It just shows you like,
"Hey, come on."

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.453
And they let you go,
"Yeah, you can stick up --"

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:08.688
I just love that story.

00:08:08.688 --> 00:08:11.356
It's cool.
And congrats again on the book.

00:08:11.356 --> 00:08:13.225
Your book is out.
Your memoir is out.

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:16.094
"Unfinished." It is out now.
Congratulations.

00:08:16.094 --> 00:08:17.363
-Thank you so much, Jimmy.

00:08:17.363 --> 00:08:19.431
-We always play a game
when you come on the show.

00:08:19.431 --> 00:08:22.201
We've done every single thing.
-And you always lose.

00:08:22.201 --> 00:08:25.404
It's so much fun.
-I almost died that one time.

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:29.041
I almost drowned myself.
-So did I. So did I.

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:30.809
-Alright, alright.
-The "Hot Ones" --

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:33.746
-That one was a rough one.
We've done a lot of stuff.

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:35.748
You almost threw yourself
through a wall once.

00:08:35.748 --> 00:08:39.318
Do you remember that one?
-Yes.

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:40.653
-It was so funny.

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:42.721
Anyways, I wanted to play
a little game

00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:44.222
with you now through Zoom.

00:08:44.222 --> 00:08:46.659
Is that okay?
-Let's do it. Let's do it.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:48.794
-More with Priyanka Chopra Jonas
when we come back, everybody.

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:50.095
Stick around.

00:08:50.095 --> 00:08:51.564
-♪ From the smoke of
the basement to the...♪

